      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I've been reading some stuff about evolutionary psychology lately and I'm curious about how different ancestral populations might have developed distinct cognitive traits. Can you give me a summary of the biological or evolutionary theories regarding how different environments might have shaped variations in things like temperament or cognitive processing speeds across different human groups? Just looking for the scientific perspective on this.",
